{"id":"9A","title":"Feasts and Special Days","part":{"n":9,"title":"Feasts and observances"},"url":"/law/09-feasts-and-observances/9a","entries":[{"id":"9A.1","text":"Passover is to be observed.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":12,"verses":"43-51"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":23,"verses":"5"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":9,"verses":"2-14"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":28,"verses":"16"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":16,"verses":"1-5"},{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":45,"verses":"21-25"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":22,"verses":"7-18"}],"citation":"Exod. 12:43-51; Lev. 23:5; Num. 9:2-14; Num. 28:16; Deut. 16:1-5; Ezek. 45:21-25; Luke 22:7-18."},{"id":"9A.2","text":"The Passover is to be a solemn observance throughout all generations.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":12,"verses":"42"}],"citation":"Exod. 12:42."},{"id":"9A.3","text":"No outsider, sojourner or hired servant shall eat of the Passover meal.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":12,"verses":"43,45"}],"citation":"Exod. 12:43, 45."},{"id":"9A.4","text":"Those unable to keep the Passover at its proper time are to keep it one month later.","refs":[{"book":"Numbers","chapter":9,"verses":"10-12"}],"citation":"Num. 9:10-12."},{"id":"9A.5","text":"The Feast of Unleavened Bread is to be celebrated the day after Passover (to eat unleavened bread seven days)","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":12,"verses":"15-20"},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":13,"verses":"6-7"},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":23,"verses":"15"},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":34,"verses":"18"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":23,"verses":"6-8"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":28,"verses":"17,25"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":16,"verses":"3-4"}],"citation":"Exod. 12:15-20; Exod. 13:6-7; Exod. 23:15; Exod. 34:18: Lev. 23:6-8; Num. 28:17,25; Deut. 16:3-4."},{"id":"9A.6","text":"Wave Sheaf offering (2nd day after Passover).","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":23,"verses":"10-14"}],"citation":"Lev. 23:10-14."},{"id":"9A.7","text":"In the first and seventh day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread there shall be an holy convocation, you shall do no servile work.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":12,"verses":"16"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":23,"verses":"7-8"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":28,"verses":"17,25"}],"citation":"Exod. 12:16; Lev. 23:7-8; Num. 28:17, 25."},{"id":"9A.8","text":"The Feast of Harvest (the first-fruits of thy labor).","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":23,"verses":"16,19"},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":34,"verses":"22,26"}],"citation":"Exod. 23:16, 19; Exod. 34:22, 26."},{"id":"9A.9","text":"The Feast of Ingathering.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":23,"verses":"16"},{"book":"Exodus","chapter":34,"verses":"22"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":23,"verses":"39-41"}],"citation":"Exod. 23:16; Exod. 34:22; Lev. 23:39-41."},{"id":"9A.10","text":"Feast of Weeks (Pentecost) -Seven weeks to be counted from the time you begin harvest, then on the fiftieth day you shall celebrate the Feast of Weeks.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":34,"verses":"22"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":23,"verses":"15-16"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":16,"verses":"9-12"}],"citation":"Exod. 34:22; Lev. 23:15-16; Deut. 16:9-12."},{"id":"9A.11","text":"Feast of Trumpets -a day for blowing the trumpets (To do no work on that day).","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":23,"verses":"24-25"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":29,"verses":"1"}],"citation":"Lev. 23:24-25; Num. 29:1."},{"id":"9A.12","text":"Feast of Tabernacles -you shall keep a feast to the LORD for seven days.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":23,"verses":"34-36,39-43"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":29,"verses":"12"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":16,"verses":"13-15"}],"citation":"Lev. 23:34-36, 39-43; Num. 29:12; Deut. 16:13-15."},{"id":"9A.13","text":"You shall celebrate the Feast of Tabernacles seven days after you have gathered in from your threshing floor and wine vat.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":16,"verses":"13-14"}],"citation":"Deut. 16:13-14."},{"id":"9A.14","text":"On the first and eighth day of the Feast of Tabernacles you shall have a sacred assembly, you shall do no customary work.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":23,"verses":"35-36,39"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":29,"verses":"35"}],"citation":"Lev. 23:35-36, 39; Num. 29:35."},{"id":"9A.15","text":"Day of Atonement - You shall humble your souls and do no work on that day.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":16,"verses":"29-34"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":23,"verses":"27-32"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":29,"verses":"7"}],"citation":"Lev. 16:29-34; Lev. 23:27-32; Num. 29:7."}]}